ger in number or amount", "to make something better"], "answer": 2}, {"question": "What does 'opportunity' mean?", "options": ["working well without wasting time", "to propose an idea", "knowledge you get from doing things", "a chance to do something"], "answer": 3}, {"question": "What does 'reduce' mean?", "options": ["to help someone", "to stay away from something", "to make something better", "to make something smaller or less"], "answer": 3}, {"question": "What does 'require' mean?", "options": ["something difficult that tests you", "to give someone support or confidence", "to need something", "to propose an idea"], "answer": 2}, {"question": "What does 'responsibility' mean?", "options": ["to successfully reach a goal", "a chance to do something", "a duty you must do", "to help someone"], "answer": 2}, {"question": "What does 'succeed' mean?", "options": ["to make something better", "to achieve success", "working well without wasting time", "something difficult that tests you"], "answer": 1}, {"question": "What does 'suggest' mean?", "options": ["to stay away from something", "very useful or important", "to propose an idea", "to successfully reach a goal"], "answer": 2}, {"question": "What does 'support' mean?", "options": ["to propose an idea", "to stay away from something", "to help someone", "an advantage or good effect"], "answer": 2}, {"question": "What does 'valuable' mean?", "options": ["working well without wasting time", "very useful or important", "something difficult that tests you", "to help someone"], "answer": 1}, {"question": "What does 'experience' mean?", "options": ["to propose an idea", "knowledge you get from doing things", "to make something better", "to successfully reach a goal"], "answer": 1}], "grammar": {"title": "1A: Present simple and continuous, action and non-action verbs", "explanation": "Use the present simple for things that are always true or happen regularly, like 'I live in Toronto' or 'She works in a bank.' For he, she, and 